  "findings": [
    {
      "evidence": "template/scripts/lifecycle_overview.py `assess_candidate`: `stage = \"merged-open-obligations\" if candidate.get(\"next_job\") or state.startswith(\"contribution\") else \"closed\"`. This branch never sees the Requirement. The correct separation exists only in `assess_requirement` (`merged_not_done`). Per-PR output, including `show --pr` and the candidate list, can therefore show `[closed]` for a merged PR whose Requirement is not Done. Contract: spec.md \"Delivery stages\" (\"a merged PR whose Requirement is not `Done` ... as `merged-open-obligations`, distinct from `closed`\"); design.md decision 3 (`closed`: PR merged with no obligation, Requirement `Done`).",
      "id": "candidate-closed-ignores-requirement-done",
      "severity": "advisory",
      "summary": "A merged PR with no open obligation is classified `closed` at candidate level without checking the parent Requirement's `Done` status. The spec and design say `closed` needs the Requirement to be `Done`, and a merged PR whose Requirement is not `Done` must be `merged-open-obligations`."
    }
  ],
